id: pm-i4kxx1
title: Accept universal SDK read receipts in the public context evaluation reader
description: "Strict compilation against the candidate packed SDK proves that PmClient cannot satisfy ContextEvaluationReader: context/next return a universal result that may contain output_budget_exceeded, even for an unbounded request when shared budgets bind. The existing documentation passes PmClient directly. A guard-aware adapter can make the example correct now, but the evaluator should compose with the public reader contract itself and refuse omitted data before grading."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T17:04:26.652Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T15:05:07.318Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-12T15:05:06.653Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-12T15:05:06.653Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Direct PmClient and structural reader integrations compile without casts; context and next results retain universal budget refusal types; infeasible or shared-budget omissions fail explicitly before scoring instead of being treated as empty ranked context; complete results preserve metrics and attribution; published Node/Bun and strict TypeScript consumers prove the contract
parent: pm-atfm
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Accept direct SDK context/next readers and refuse omitted results before grading, preserving metrics, token accounting and served attribution."
expected_result: Real PmClient and structural readers compose without casts; infeasible receipts never score as empty success.
actual_result: "All 10295 functional assertions and exact 100/100/100/100 source coverage passed. Five linked commands pass, including installed Node/Bun, strict TypeScript and npm/npx/Bun/bunx. Corrected head 7411d7ee6 passes all 26 required contexts, including real native Windows Bun acceptance."
